<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Libandla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Libandla is the general national council of the Swazi, an assembly of chiefs, councillors and other men that the king traditionally consulted on matters affecting the nation. Its name is also used for the modern Parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a>. Together with the smaller inner council, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liqoqo">Liqoqo</a>, it formed part of the system through which the Swazi monarchy governed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/libandla.jpg" alt="Libandla" width="245" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: New International Church · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parliament_of_Eswatini.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
